<title>HUNGARY: Hamburg Airlines to start Budapest-Dresden flights.</title>
<headline>Hamburg Airlines to start Budapest-Dresden flights.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German regional airline Hamburg Airlines plans to start non-stop flights between Budapest and Dresden on March 31 with turbo-prop DASH-8-300 airplanes, Hungary's Airport Coordination Service (ACS) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The flights, scheduled once a day Monday to Friday  until October 24, seat 50 passengers with little room for cargo, ACS's general airport coordinator, Helen Guraly, told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Ryan Tutak, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
